    "input": "Natural An, n>=12, actual string C-marking, a transitive maximal omission H preserving two blocks, every distinguished maximal omission H_j intransitive.",
    "finite_bases": "Exact finite maxima settle n<=14. A row-swapping even involution then gives n=2m with even m>=8.",
    "empty_R": "Actual IP makes the commuting remainder faithful on the l-pairs. Its genuine transitive rank>=m-2 action is Sm or Am by complete L047 including m8, proving maximality before the completed pair-block theorem is invoked.",
    "nonempty_R": "The complete contracted forest gives r<=m. A rank failure forces r=m. R1 preserving is excluded; R1 swapping changes the distinguished block swap and enters R2 with every standing hypothesis retained.",
    "two_neighbours": "The common full graph reduction gives connected4pair core. Both-preserving and at-least-one-swapping are separately complete and exhaust all cases.",
    "acyclicity": "Neither two-neighbour proof uses a completed one-neighbour exclusion. The one-neighbour swap is only routing to R2. The completed pair-block theorem is independent of this binary omission branch and uses only explicitly assumed smaller alternating degrees.",
    "induction": "Alternating bound floor((q-1)/2) in every12<=q<n is a stated theorem hypothesis; lower exact finite maxima are acquired."
